# FINAL STUDENT PROFILE

After the five forms, the system should conceptually have:

```text
PAST
├── Academic background
├── Strong subjects
├── Academic level
└── Entrance-exam status

PRESENT
├── Interests
├── Work preferences
├── Learning preferences
└── Current activities

CURRENT SITUATION
├── College status
├── Budget preference
├── Location/relocation
├── Priorities
└── Available time

GOAL
├── Career destination
├── Goal certainty
├── Motivation
└── Definition of success

SKILLS
├── Existing skills
├── Self-assessed levels
├── Project experience
└── Learning independence
```

This profile becomes the input to the AI engine.

---

# WHAT HAPPENS AFTER FORM 5?

The system should NOT immediately tell the student:

> “This is your best career.”

Instead:

## STEP 1 — AI analyses current state

```text
Where is the student now?
```

↓

## STEP 2 — AI identifies relevant gaps

```text
What is missing between current state and goal?
```

↓

## STEP 3 — AI generates 2–3 genuinely different routes

```text
Different education/skill/entry strategies
→
Same desired destination
```

↓

## STEP 4 — Student compares routes

Each route should show:

* Degree/education route
* Specialization
* Timeline
* Skills required
* Projects
* Internship strategy
* Estimated effort
* Relevant constraints
* Trade-offs
* Why it fits the student

↓

## STEP 5 — Student chooses a route

↓

## STEP 6 — Product converts route into an actionable journey

```text
Long-term goal
↓
Milestones
↓
Monthly objectives
↓
Weekly objectives
↓
Daily missions
```

↓

## STEP 7 — Progress tracking

* Completed tasks
* Skill progress
* Streak
* Milestones
* Roadmap completion

